  Where this leaves your original request: nothing about notifications has been designed yet, by design. This cycle
  produces the [38;5;153mtask_events[39m log and [38;5;153mGET /api/events[39m that notifications will consume, plus the watcher table that answers
  "tasks they care about." Delivery channels, read/unread state, digesting, and per-user preferences are all deferred to
  the notifications spec, which gets its own brainstorm once there's a real event stream to design against.

  Please review the spec and tell me if you want changes. Once you approve it, the next step is the writing-plans skill
  to turn it into an implementation plan — no code before then.

